/* expr — a tiny recursive-descent parser and evaluator.

   Grammar:  expr   := term { "+" term }
             term   := factor { "*" factor }
             factor := number | "(" expr ")"

   Nodes are a closed union of three object types; eval dispatches with
   Judge and needs no Otherwise, because the checker can see the union is
   covered. The parser is an object whose methods recurse through each
   other: parse-expr -> parse-term -> parse-factor -> parse-expr.

   Kids live in a catalogue — a series whose element type is the union —
   because a recursive shape needs a container's indirection to close, and
   the container's element type must admit every node kind. */

Define object num-node with (the number value).
Define object add-node with (the catalogue of (num-node or add-node or mul-node) kids).
Define object mul-node with (the catalogue of (num-node or add-node or mul-node) kids).

Bind series of text to tokenize, given (the text src):
    Define tokens as a series of text.
    Define total as the length of src.
    Define i as 1.
    While i is not greater than total, repeat:
        Define ch as the characters from i to i of src.
        If ch is " ", i becomes i + 1.
        Otherwise if ch is "+" or ch is "*" or ch is "(" or ch is ")":
            Add ch to tokens.
            The i becomes i + 1.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Define num-start as i.
            While i is not greater than total, repeat:
                Define d as the characters from i to i of src.
                If "0123456789" contains d, i becomes i + 1.
                Otherwise, stop.
            Done.
            Define num-text as the characters from num-start to i - 1 of src.
            Add num-text to tokens.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return tokens.
Done.

Define object parser with (the series of text tokens, the number pos):
    Bind text to peek:
        If one's pos is greater than the number of one's tokens, return "<end>".
        Define here as one's pos.
        Return item here of one's tokens.
    Done.

    Bind void to advance:
        One's pos becomes one's pos + 1.
    Done.

    Bind (num-node or add-node or mul-node) or failure to parse-expr:
        Define node as cast one's parse-term or pass the failure off.
        While (cast one's peek) is "+", repeat:
            Cast one's advance.
            Define right as cast one's parse-term or pass the failure off.
            The node becomes a new add-node { the kids a catalogue of (num-node or add-node or mul-node) with (node, right) }.
        Done.
        Return node.
    Done.

    Bind (num-node or add-node or mul-node) or failure to parse-term:
        Define node as cast one's parse-factor or pass the failure off.
        While (cast one's peek) is "*", repeat:
            Cast one's advance.
            Define right as cast one's parse-factor or pass the failure off.
            The node becomes a new mul-node { the kids a catalogue of (num-node or add-node or mul-node) with (node, right) }.
        Done.
        Return node.
    Done.

    Bind (num-node or add-node or mul-node) or failure to parse-factor:
        Define head as cast one's peek.
        If head is "(":
            Cast one's advance.
            Define inner as cast one's parse-expr or pass the failure off.
            Define closer as cast one's peek.
            If closer is not ")", return a failure "expected )".
            Cast one's advance.
            Return inner.
        Done.
        Define num-value as head converted to number.
        If num-value is void, return a failure "expected a number".
        Cast one's advance.
        Return a new num-node { the value num-value }.
    Done.

    Bind (num-node or add-node or mul-node) or failure to parse-all:
        Define node as cast one's parse-expr or pass the failure off.
        Define tail as cast one's peek.
        If tail is not "<end>", return a failure "unexpected token after expression".
        Return node.
    Done.
Done.

Bind number to eval, given (the (num-node or add-node or mul-node) node):
    Judge node, where it is:
        A num-node, return the value of it.
        An add-node:
            Define kids as the kids of it.
            Define left-kid as the first of kids.
            Define right-kid as item 2 of kids.
            Return cast eval on (left-kid) + cast eval on (right-kid).
        Done.
        A mul-node:
            Define kids as the kids of it.
            Define left-kid as the first of kids.
            Define right-kid as item 2 of kids.
            Return cast eval on (left-kid) * cast eval on (right-kid).
        Done.
    Done.
Done.

Bind void to demo, given (the text src):
    Define tokens as cast tokenize on (src).
    Define p as a new parser { the tokens tokens, the pos 1 }.
    Try to:
        Define tree as cast p's parse-all.
        Define answer as cast eval on (tree).
        State "{src} = {answer converted to text}".
    Done.
    In case of failure:
        State "{src} -> {the message of the failure}".
    Done.
Done.

Bind void to play:
    Cast demo on ("2 + 3 * 4").
    Cast demo on ("(2 + 3) * 4").
    Cast demo on ("2 * (3 + 4) + 1").
    Cast demo on ("2 + ").
    Cast demo on ("2 ) 3").
Done.

Cast play.